Theorem DP-2: is_rc_dec_unnecessary truth table — Absent OR Dead

  Preconditions:
    - s is a canonical AimsState per Annex E §AIMS product lattice
    - is_rc_dec_unnecessary : AimsState -> Bool per Annex E §AIMS DP-2
      + Appendix C truth table
    - CN-1 invariant (Annex E §AIMS CN-1): Consumption = Dead <=>
      Cardinality = Absent bidirectional; canonical states satisfy the
      bidirectional equivalence
    - DP-2 gates SUPPLEMENTARY RC ops ONLY — terminal RL-2 / RL-4 / RL-5
      definitional cleanup decs own their own logic per Annex E §AIMS
      RL-2 (DP-2 NEVER suppresses cleanup decs on UNUSED owned non-scalar
      values)

  Soundness property:
    Forall s in AimsState (canonical, post-CN-1).
      is_rc_dec_unnecessary(s)
        <=> (s.cardinality = Absent OR s.consumption = Dead)

    Under CN-1 the two clauses are bidirectionally implied; canonical
    states satisfying either satisfy both. The disjunction is therefore
    equivalent to (s.cardinality = Absent AND s.consumption = Dead) on
    canonical states.

  Proof obligation:
    Three-part discharge:
      (a) Enumerate the 4 Consumption x 3 Cardinality = 12 product states.
      (b) Apply CN-1 canonical filter: skip the 5 infeasible combinations
          (Dead AND != Absent: 2 states; != Dead AND Absent: 3 states).
          Remaining canonical subset: 7 states.
      (c) For each canonical row, verify the predicate value equals the
          Appendix C row partition value.

    Part (a) — Appendix C row partition (4 rows, exhaustive):
      Row 1: Cardinality = Absent (under CN-1 forces Dead) -> true
        Soundness: predicate true (first disjunct holds).
      Row 2: any Cardinality, Consumption = Dead (under CN-1 forces Absent)
          -> true
        Soundness: predicate true (second disjunct holds).
      Row 3: Cardinality = Once, Consumption != Dead -> false
        Soundness: predicate false (neither disjunct holds).
      Row 4: Cardinality = Many, Consumption != Dead -> false
        Soundness: predicate false (neither disjunct holds).

    Part (b) — CN-1 canonical filter:
      Product cardinality: 4 x 3 = 12.
      Infeasible (eliminated by CN-1):
        - Consumption = Dead AND Cardinality in {Once, Many}: 2 states.
        - Consumption in {Linear, Affine, Unrestricted} AND Cardinality =
          Absent: 3 states.
      Canonical subset: 12 - 5 = 7 states.
        Canonical rows: (Dead, Absent),
                       (Linear, Once), (Linear, Many),
                       (Affine, Once), (Affine, Many),
                       (Unrestricted, Once), (Unrestricted, Many).

    Part (c) — soundness equality on canonical rows:
      Canonical row (Dead, Absent) -> DP-2 = true (Appendix Row 1 AND Row 2).
      Canonical rows (!= Dead, Once / Many) -> DP-2 = false (Appendix
        Row 3 / 4).
      Negative-direction witness: DP-2 = true on EXACTLY the (Dead, Absent)
      canonical row; the 6 other canonical rows return false.

    DP-2 gating clarification (success_criterion §05.1):
      DP-2 gates supplementary RC-op tracking ONLY. RL-2 cleanup decs on
      UNUSED owned non-scalar values (Cardinality = Absent OR Consumption =
      Dead) are emitted by the definitional-cleanup rule itself per
      Annex E §AIMS RL-2 "RL-2 includes UNUSED owned non-scalar values".
      DP-2 NEVER suppresses cleanup decs; it gates additional supplementary
      RC ops beyond the terminal RL-2 / RL-4 / RL-5 emissions.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — 12-product / 7-canonical enumeration per
        section_05::verify_dp2_rc_dec_unnecessary; the verifier applies the
        CN-1 canonical filter and checks the soundness equality on every
        canonical row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_05 case_analysis engine discharges DP-2 via 12-product / 7-canonical-post-CN-1 enumeration per Annex E §AIMS DP-2 + Appendix C + §2 CN-1
